I made no changes to my language's grammar during this lab. In this lab, I created a new Java class
called parser that would take in a list of tokens and parse through it using some of the grammar
rules we discussed in class. We would take a token and go through the rules from expression to equality
to comparison to term to factor to unary to primary. 

My test cases went through a variety of different scenarios, including testing strings, numbers, unary expressions
, a binary expression with more unary, term, and factor. I also added some comparison expressions to help represent
a variety of cases there. Even including a string inside the comparison, which would not normally be
valid, but for now it is still a valid expression. 

